 is bar 14, not bar 16, since bar 16 ends with Bb3 dotted quarter and Ab3 quarter. One possible mismatch: the 2nd and 3rd of the rising 8ths look higher than Ab4 and C5, maybe C5 and Eb5. It could be a copyist's variant or my misreading of the image. The bar's identity holds either way.\n\nLast stretch (after the barline at x 1665): Eb5 dotted 8th, F5 16th, Db5 8th, grace note, C5 quarter, Bb4 8th, then the line ends. \"rinf\" is written above. That is the first half of bar 15; the next line finishes the bar.\n\nSo the line holds bars 12, 13, 14 and part of 15.","right":true,"insights":"Easy to place overall: the repeated low C4 bar (13) and the endings of the bars (bar 14 ends with a rest, bar 16 with a dotted quarter) separate bars 12, 13 and 14 from the look-alike bars 15 and 16. The faint barlines and the small, unclear note heads in the rising 8ths were harder. A sharper image, or bar numbers in the part, would have made the decision quicker."},"ttft_ms":9464,"type":"result","duration_ms":30009,"uuid":"c4d9701f-604e-4dca-8650-b555ef35a2e2","ttft_stream_ms":1636,"time_to_request_ms":400,"first_content_frame_ms":1636,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2718,"cacheReadInputTokens":1046,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11429,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1460172,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1929,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":11429,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
